values.script:2:1: bad size "0x24" (columns must be 1 to 1000)
values.script:3:1: duplicate "size" (first set on line 2)
values.script:3:1: bad size "80" (write COLSxROWS, for example 80x24)
values.script:4:1: bad seed "-1" (a seed is a whole number, 0 or more)
values.script:5:1: bad jitter "150%" (jitter is 0% to 100%)
values.script:6:1: "jitter" is set twice with no step between (the value on line 5 is never used)
values.script:6:1: bad jitter "25" (a percentage is a number with %, like 25%)
values.script:7:1: bad speed "0x" (speed is 0.001x to 1000000x)
values.script:8:1: bad duration "50" (a duration needs a unit: ms, s or m (for example 50s))
values.script:9:1: bad timeout "0s" (timeout must be greater than 0)
